course: dictionary
lesson: 15070
title: Rico: a name, a place, a Spanish word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are hard to find in an English dictionary because they are not English. Start with clues. A capital letter at the start is a big clue: «Rico» with a capital R is often a person's name or part of a place name.
explain: «Puerto Rico is an island in the Caribbean.» Here rico is part of a place name, so you learn what the whole name means, not just one word. In this name, rico is not a word you need to translate on its own.
explain: «Rico scored the winning goal in the playground match.» Rico is a boy's name, and it is often short for Ricardo or Enrico. When a sentence tells you what someone did, you know it is a person.
explain: Rico is also a Spanish word, meaning rich or tasty. It is not an English word, so an English dictionary may not show it. Check the language first, then the meaning.
fact: Rico is usually part of the place name Puerto Rico.
fact: Puerto Rico is an island in the Caribbean that belongs to the USA.
fact: Rico is a boy's name, often short for Ricardo or Enrico.
fact: In Spanish, «rico» means rich or tasty, but it is not an English word.
fact: A capital letter at the start of a word often means it is a name for a person or place.
exercise: «Rico kicked the ball and ran to the goal.» What is Rico in this sentence? | *A boy's name | A kind of fruit | A town in Spain | A type of boat
exercise: Ms Bell says, «We are learning about Puerto Rico in geography.» What is Puerto Rico? | *An island in the Caribbean that belongs to the USA | A river in Spain | A king from long ago | A kind of sweet food
exercise: Maria says in Spanish, «La sopa es rico.» What does rico mean? | *Rich or tasty | Very fast | The name of a dog | Cold and wet
test: Rico is often short for which two names? | Rachel or Rosa | Ricky or Rory | Mario or Luis | *Ricardo or Enrico
test: Is rico an English word? | Yes, it means very rich in English | Yes, it means a small boat | Yes, it is a kind of tree | *No, it is a Spanish word
exam: «Jo said, Rico is my cousin and he lives in Puerto Rico.» What tells you that Rico is a name here? | It is the name of a colour | It rhymes with a type of fish | *The capital R and the fact that he is a person | It is the name of a month
